## 1. MVVM Clean Architecture Diagrams

### Layered Architecture Flowchart

The diagram below illustrates how data and control flow between the **UI Layer**, **Domain Layer**, and **Data Layer**.

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph UI_Layer ["1. UI Layer (Presentation)"]
        View["Jetpack Compose Screen (@Composable)"]
        VM["MVVM ViewModel (Hilt Injected)"]
        State["UiState (StateFlow / Sealed Interface)"]
        Event["UiEvent (User Actions / Callbacks)"]
    end

    subgraph Domain_Layer ["2. Domain Layer (Pure Business Logic)"]
        UC["Use Cases (e.g. GetUserProfileUseCase)"]
        Model["Domain Models (Pure Kotlin Data Classes)"]
    end

    subgraph Data_Layer ["3. Data Layer (Single Source of Truth)"]
        Repo["UserRepositoryImpl"]
        Remote["Remote DataSource (Retrofit API)"]
        Local["Local DataSource (Room DB)"]
    end

    %% Flow interactions
    View -- "1. Emits User Event" --> Event
    Event -- "2. Triggers Event Function" --> VM
    VM -- "3. Executes Use Case" --> UC
    UC -- "4. Requests Data" --> Repo
    Repo -- "5a. Fetches API Data" --> Remote
    Repo -- "5b. Caches / Queries Local DB" --> Local
    Repo -- "6. Returns Domain Model" --> UC
    UC -- "7. Delivers Result" --> VM
    VM -- "8. Updates StateFlow" --> State
    State -- "9. Recomposes UI" --> View

    %% Styling
    classDef uiStyle fill:#f2fbf5,stroke:#008544,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef domainStyle fill:#eff6ff,stroke:#2563eb,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef dataStyle fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706,stroke-width:2px;

    class View,VM,State,Event uiStyle;
    class UC,Model domainStyle;
    class Repo,Remote,Local dataStyle;
```

